  "id": "binaural-summation-effect",
  "term": "binaural summation effect",
  "definition": "The binaural summation effect is the improved performance that can occur when sound information from both ears is combined rather than heard with one ear alone. In this packet, it refers to a measure of binaural benefit in speech understanding, including in bimodal listening with a cochlear implant in one ear and a hearing aid in the other.",
